class Solution {
    public int passwordStrength(String password) {
        // Set to track characters we've already seen
        Set<Character> seen = new HashSet<>();

        // Define a set of special characters that give extra score
        Set<Character> special = Set.of('!','@','#','$');

        // Iterate through each character in the password
        for (char ch : password.toCharArray()) {
            // Only process if this character hasn't been seen before
            if (seen.add(ch)) {
                // If lowercase letter → add 1 point
                if (Character.isLowerCase(ch)) {
                    score += 1;
                }
                // If uppercase letter → add 2 points
                if (Character.isUpperCase(ch)) {
                    score += 2;
                }
                // If digit → add 3 points
                if (Character.isDigit(ch)) {
                    score += 3;
                }
                // If special character from our set → add 5 points
                if (special.contains(ch)) {
                    score += 5;
                }
            }
        }
        return score;
    }
}

Time Complexity: 
𝑂(𝑛) — proportional to password length.

Space Complexity: 
𝑂(1).
